92-- **Research: no Texas overlay on federal §366 for gas.** Neither Utilities Code nor RRC Chapter 7 adds bankruptcy-specific provisions. Implement federally: 20-day adequate-assurance (individual Ch. 7/13), 30-day (Ch. 11, six enumerated assurance forms); deposit-as-adequate-assurance; disconnect permitted after window if assurance not furnished. Ordinary Texas holds (EWE, seriously-ill, payment plans) run independently and can overlap. Pairs with D8-2's event-terminated model.
93-
94-### Family 11 — Texas sub-jurisdiction/rate-change, bill format/read cadence
95-- **D11-1: Missed newspaper-notice week → full reset.** Fresh four-week run, fresh 35-day clock from new first publication. "Four consecutive weeks" — a gap breaks consecutiveness; conservative reading because wrong-toward-lenient = premature rate application (refund + penalty), wrong-toward-conservative = calendar delay. Platform tracks publication dates, computes earliest effective date, warns on gaps.
96-- **Research (Q-8 closed): bilingual = statewide English/Spanish standard** (16 TAC §7.45(2)(A)(vi), §7.45(4)(C)), "as necessary to adequately inform," good-cause Spanish exemption available on application. No border-county multi-language mandate. **Design: two-language enum + per-tenant "exemption on file" flag. No county table.** Axis A4 unblocks as drafted.
--
