118-### Session 3A — reads, validation, estimation
119:- **D3A-1 (scope correction, supersedes earlier in-session framing): `photo_ai` is ON HOLD.** It was conceived as a field-tech phone-app capability (photograph meter while resolving tickets, OCR extracts read); the feature is held because the ticketing/field-service layer is being kept platform-agnostic. → Deferral register. Read-VEE table drops the `photo_ai` row entirely; no OCR-confidence column in v5.4. **The only photo-adjacent v1 behavior:** CSR-requested photo during a service interaction → attaches to the case as evidence → employee enters/confirms the read of record. Never a read source. **No customer-initiated reads in v1, period.** Design note for when the hold lifts: platform-agnostic ticketing means the eventual field app submits reads through the same external-read API surface any third-party field tool would use — no privileged internal channel.
120-- **D3A-2: VEE thresholds (150% prior-year spike / 10% class-average low-usage) ship as tenant-configurable starter defaults**, explicitly marked "tune per tenant," with exception-queue hit-rate reporting to support tuning. No canonical industry number exists.
121-- **D3A-3: `meter_skip_reason` enum → v5.4.** Set: `no_access`, `locked_gate`, `dog`, `hazard`, `meter_damaged`, `customer_refused`, `weather`, `other`+notes.
122-- **D3A-4: Tamper recording columns → v5.4** (`tamper_flag`, `tamper_reported_at`, reason/source on meter or read record). Feeds the Critical portlet. **Algorithmic tamper detection from consumption patterns = v2 analytics, deferred.**
