124-### Session 3B — gas measurement, meter lifecycle
125-- **D3B-1: Pressure-factor carry-forward validation on meter swaps — build it, fired AFTER the pressure test.** Sequence: meter set → pressure test → result establishes effective Fp → validation compares against service point's last-known Fp → mismatch requires explicit operator confirmation with reason before swap commits / meter goes billable. Silent + financial + permanent fails the operator-training test.
126-- **D3B-2: Activation QA gate — measurement-critical attributes must be affirmed, never defaulted.** Zone assignment and pressure class carry `confirmed_at`/`confirmed_by` at activation; the pressure-test result is what affirms pressure for the gate. D3B-1 and D3B-2 share one checkpoint, not two hurdles.
127-- **D3B-3: Sewer → explicit tracked deferral** (same pattern as Q-12 transport-balancing). Out of v1 scenario scope; revisit at multi-commodity launch.
